WEBVTT

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:05.920
The enemy?

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:10.420
The alchemy of Carol Malus Dienheim

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:12.610
will destroy the world

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:15.610
and complete the Apocalypse of All Things.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:17.780
Destroy the world?

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:21.040
I am going to slay a miracle.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:43.730
Why don't you equip your Symphogear?

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:45.690
Why don't you fight?

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:47.610
Instead of fighting...

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:51.480
Tell me why you want to destroy the world!

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:05.500
If I tell you why, will you accept my reason?

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:07.770
I...

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:10.380
I don't want to fight!

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:15.030
Unlike you, there's a truth I desire,

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:16.760
even if it means fighting!

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:15.960
<b>Episode 2 
Before I Destroy the World</b>

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:15.960
I thought we were all having a sleepover.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:18.520
We can't be messing around

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:21.180
while Tachibana-san and 
Hibiki-san are working hard.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:23.750
I'm just glad Hina had a spare key

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:26.020
to Kinekuri-senpai's house.

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:27.850
But why did you have one?

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.500
Oh, hmm...

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:32.280
Why, I wonder.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:34.980
Maybe Hibiki gave it to me.

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:38.480
Okay, okay! Senpais...

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.910
We'll be heading home!

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:42.950
Thanks for inviting us.

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:44.280
Bye!

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:44.910
Kiri-chan!

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:46.860
Bye-bye!

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:48.330
Take care!

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:53.000
Okay, maybe I'll go buy a rice ball 
at the convenience store.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:54.070
Oh, my.

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:55.160
My, my.

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:57.920
I thought you'd be worried.

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:01.450
Hibiki's hobby is saving people. She'll be fine.

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:05.200
I'm more worried that she'll come home hungry.

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:15.210
Thanks to Hibiki-chan, rescue efforts 
at the burning condos are going well.

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:18.610
I can't let her have all the glory.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:37.790
Was that you?

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:46.760
<i>Is that...</i>

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:48.760
The Symphogear-wielder transport was destroyed!

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:50.370
What's going on?

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:52.430
It seems someone attacked it.

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:55.940
We've also got a message from London 
that Tsubasa-san is under attack.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:57.830
<i>Simultaneous attacks?</i>

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.360
<i>Are they trying to confuse us?</i>

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:01.710
<i>But still...</i>

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:03.990
Ogawa...

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:05.610
Yes?

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:09.740
At this rate, information will overwhelm us, 
and we won't learn what they're after.

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:11.200
Understood.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.770
I'll contact Scotland Yard and MI5 for help,

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:15.430
and try to figure out what's going on.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:28.460
I'm ready.

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:30.780
If you say so...

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:33.810
Then we'll do this fair and square.

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:37.060
Don't go whining later!

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:44.860
<i>Killiter Ichaival tron.</i>

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:25.810
<i>Those movements...</i>

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:27.400
<i>Those aren't just beyond human capabilities.</i>

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:28.900
<i>She's a monster!</i>

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:34.090
In other words, that makes 
her easier to deal with!

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:35.440
Commander...

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:36.380
What is it?

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:38.580
Do you think this has something

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:41.750
to do with that mysterious 
signal we saw last night?

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:45.800
An unidentified signal waveform 
and a new enemy...

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.920
One of the highest-level phonic gains and 
combat abilities of the Symphogear-wielders,

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:59.390
and it isn't enough to damage Leiur.

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:03.110
I need to deliver Dvergr Dáinn's legacy, after all.

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:24.250
A direct hit?

00:07:29.850 --> 00:07:32.380
I'd heard your songs were far better than that.

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:36.890
Indeed, I certainly cannot let 
you beat me with that.

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:46.810
Did you get her?

00:07:46.810 --> 00:07:48.030
Not at all.

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:49.990
I just knocked her down below.

00:07:53.230 --> 00:07:54.880
Let's go, Tsubasa!

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:05.080
Stop wasting my time and come out already!

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:14.010
What happened, Chris-chan?

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:16.510
The enemy! An enemy attack!

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:17.930
What's happening there?

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:19.720
Watch out!

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:26.230
What kind of joke is this?!

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:40.120
Plain doesn't suit me.

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:43.500
But this is a touch too fancy...

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:47.320
Any more, and I simply become plain.

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:54.700
Now, then...

00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:04.100
You guys, stay here!

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:06.810
We can't let you go out there without LiNKER!

00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:10.360
<i>Come to think of it, that's natural.</i>

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:14.110
They may not look it, but they're 
extremely kind people.

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:16.990
After the Frontier Incident,

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:20.590
the ones who took us in were

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:23.380
the ones we'd fought as enemies.

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:23.700
<b>Starting in spring, 
we'll be in the same school.</b>

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:27.040
It may be that we're on probation,

00:09:27.510 --> 00:09:29.880
but they're letting us go to school.

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:32.550
Hey? Why so scared?

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:33.810
Hey!

00:09:33.810 --> 00:09:35.050
Good morning!

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:37.970
If you don't hurry, you'll be late!

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:48.600
We couldn't have even imagined 
all the fun we're having

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:51.110
back when we were in the FIS research facility.

00:09:57.480 --> 00:10:00.890
Is there some way we could get 
the power to help them?

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:04.610
I want to help them, somehow.

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:09.470
The power to do so is right here, of course.

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:13.940
But until today, we weren't able to change

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:16.810
anything with that alone, Kiri-chan.

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:21.430
<b>Breaking: High-Rise Condo Fire in City Center</b>

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:19.410
<i>And now an update on the fire that broke out</i>

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:21.430
<i>in high-rise condos and surrounding 
city-center areas.</i>

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:25.930
<i>The scene is still chaotic, but there have been 
continued sightings of a suspicious person,</i>

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:28.810
<b>Breaking: High-Rise Condo Fire in City Center</b>

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:28.360
<i>and some believe it may be terrorism.</i>

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:30.600
That was...

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:32.770
An explosion in mid-air!

00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:36.940
Something else may be going on.

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:44.090
What a mess she made!

00:10:44.670 --> 00:10:45.900
Are you okay?

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:46.740
Yeah.

00:10:47.900 --> 00:10:50.100
You—that outfit...

00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:51.500
You...

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:55.310
I'm Little Red Riding Gun,

00:10:55.310 --> 00:10:57.920
a superhero with absolutely no connection 
to the UN or Japanese government,

00:10:57.920 --> 00:10:59.380
who fights day and night to save—

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:01.490
Yukine Chris-san, wielder of the

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:03.680
Ichaival Symphogear, yes?

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:06.170
That voice...

00:11:06.170 --> 00:11:07.990
You're the one who saved me!

00:11:10.550 --> 00:11:12.470
My name is Elfnein.

00:11:12.470 --> 00:11:15.380
I've been searching for you all,

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:17.150
to save the world from Carol's alchemy.

00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:21.950
Did you say "alchemy"?

00:11:26.340 --> 00:11:27.490
Alchemy...

00:11:28.190 --> 00:11:31.810
Does she mean the over-technology 
that existed before

00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:34.000
science and magic split into different fields?

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:36.900
That means our new threat is a different type

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:39.340
of heretical technology than the Symphogear.

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:43.070
A new enemy.

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:45.420
An alchemist.

00:11:48.190 --> 00:11:51.770
How do I sell footage like this to a TV station?

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:54.520
You shouldn't videotape someone 
without their permission.

00:11:55.750 --> 00:11:58.550
Shows how badly you've been raised.

00:12:13.970 --> 00:12:16.460
A truth you want, even if it means fighting?

00:12:16.760 --> 00:12:19.820
Yes. You have one, as well?

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:23.720
That's why you stopped the Moon's 
destruction with your songs.

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:26.490
With your songs, with your Symphogear,

00:12:26.490 --> 00:12:27.850
you fought!

00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:29.090
No!

00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:31.620
I had to, that's all.

00:12:31.970 --> 00:12:33.910
I didn't want to...

00:12:34.660 --> 00:12:37.310
I didn't want to fight!

00:12:38.060 --> 00:12:41.360
I wanted to protect people with my Symphogear!

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:44.800
Fight anyway.

00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:49.870
Do what you have the power to do!

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:54.120
I don't want to fight using a power 
that's meant to save people...

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:59.050
Then you'll try to save people 
and get killed, too?!

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:01.630
High-level energy output!

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:04.550
Why doesn't she fight in the 
presence of the enemy?

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:06.360
Send reinforcements!

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:09.920
No, if they aren't Noise, I'll go.

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:11.680
Send our HQ forces there now!

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:15.480
No! Without you here, our chain 
of command will break down!

00:13:19.430 --> 00:13:20.420
But...

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:23.860
Just a moment ago, you were crying.

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:25.490
Instead of fighting,

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:28.820
I need to find out why!

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:32.180
She saw me. She knows.

00:13:32.180 --> 00:13:33.460
She got too close to me.

00:13:35.590 --> 00:13:36.830
I'll destroy you!

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:42.840
And the world!

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:46.930
Spatial distortion detected!

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:48.340
It's an unidentified energy type!

00:13:48.630 --> 00:13:49.830
Hibiki-chan, are you okay?

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:51.850
Hibiki-chan! Hibiki-chan!

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:12.410
Why do you want to destroy the world?

00:14:12.890 --> 00:14:15.490
It's the challenge my father left me.

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:18.420
You should have something like that, too.

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:21.340
Your father?

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:24.670
What a pain you can be...

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:27.700
You were watching?

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:30.430
That's just like you, Garie. 
Rotten to the core.

00:14:32.980 --> 00:14:35.010
Don't say that...

00:14:35.010 --> 00:14:38.190
You're the one who made me this way.

00:14:38.650 --> 00:14:40.860
How is the memory collection going?

00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:42.370
Just fine.

00:14:42.370 --> 00:14:46.690
But Micha-chan's inside the orb, so it's no fun!

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:48.110
Then hurry.

00:14:48.110 --> 00:14:49.750
We're leaving.

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:51.180
Roger!

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:53.580
Garie will do her best.

00:14:58.720 --> 00:15:00.850
Goodbye.

00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:04.880
Fight next time.

00:15:05.620 --> 00:15:09.620
Or I can't destroy everything you have.

00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:24.500
Entrusted...

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:27.550
My father

00:15:27.850 --> 00:15:30.570
never gave me

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:32.610
anything...

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:38.700
Recover Hibiki-chan immediately!

00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:43.140
<i>What is this strange feeling I have 
that something is wrong?</i>

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:47.920
We're confirming the situation now.

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:50.750
Seal exits A3 to A6 immediately.

00:15:52.640 --> 00:15:54.220
Agent Maria...

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:58.220
Your actions are supposed to be limited 
by the protection program!

00:15:58.610 --> 00:16:01.450
This is an emergency. We're borrowing this car.

00:16:02.780 --> 00:16:04.360
We can't allow you to do that!

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:09.190
What?

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:10.860
I can't move...

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:12.860
<b>Shadow Weave</b>

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:14.370
Ogawa-san!

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:16.800
Sorry, but I'm doing what I want with Tsubasa!

00:16:22.310 --> 00:16:23.680
What's going on?

00:16:24.240 --> 00:16:25.630
What?

00:16:25.940 --> 00:16:28.880
That idiot got beaten by the attacker?

00:16:29.290 --> 00:16:31.300
It seems Tsubasa-san and Maria-san

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:33.550
have fallen back and are regrouping, too.

00:16:35.110 --> 00:16:38.680
Is this alchemy stuff more powerful 
than a Symphogear?

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:41.330
I've got a 252 here, as well.

00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:42.430
Tell me where to rendezvous.

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:53.300
What the hell?

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:57.570
Tsubasa-san, what's going on?

00:16:57.570 --> 00:16:58.850
I'm sorry.

00:16:59.380 --> 00:17:01.430
It seems like Maria has an idea.

00:17:01.430 --> 00:17:03.070
I'll leave the concert hall to you.

00:17:04.550 --> 00:17:06.850
I'd like an explanation.

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:08.970
Think back.

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:14.790
I have been waiting for you.

00:17:15.520 --> 00:17:17.670
Without a doubt,

00:17:17.670 --> 00:17:19.810
you're the one she's after.

00:17:20.740 --> 00:17:23.060
The best way to minimize damage is

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:25.930
to get you as far away from crowds as possible.

00:17:25.930 --> 00:17:29.020
Then we should be cooperating with the others!

00:17:30.140 --> 00:17:33.310
I'm bearing some big restrictions of my own.

00:17:36.230 --> 00:17:38.710
You want me to lie even more?

00:17:39.560 --> 00:17:41.850
We're asking you to use your fame

00:17:41.850 --> 00:17:48.040
to play a role that will resolve this matter
 as peacefully as possible.

00:17:48.360 --> 00:17:50.100
Play a role?

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:53.010
The true identity of the songstress Maria

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:55.470
is that of an agent working for us, the UN.

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:58.630
You were infiltrating the anarchists

00:17:58.630 --> 00:18:02.160
to prevent them from misusing the relics.

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:08.080
It's better for the public to have a nice, 
comprehensible hero story like this.

00:18:08.380 --> 00:18:11.820
So I must return to being a false idol?

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:13.260
A false idol?

00:18:13.260 --> 00:18:15.800
Yes. An idol.

00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:18.700
If a heroine idol holds charity concerts

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:21.900
across the world, it'll also be good propaganda.

00:18:23.130 --> 00:18:25.450
It seems that the US government used Echelon

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:27.520
to back-trace all the related data

00:18:27.520 --> 00:18:31.490
and erase it from every network,

00:18:31.490 --> 00:18:33.540
including individual PCs.

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:40.840
But both she and the minors who worked 
with you have their futures to think of.

00:18:42.380 --> 00:18:44.660
What I'm saying is that, even without your Gear,

00:18:44.960 --> 00:18:49.270
you can still fight for someone else's sake.

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:52.110
<i>Even so,</i>

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:55.040
<i>I won't let something like that be my fight!</i>

00:18:58.110 --> 00:18:59.110
Maria!

00:19:14.990 --> 00:19:21.620
<i>Imyuteus Ame no Habakiri tron.</i>

00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:10.070
We may both have swords,

00:20:10.070 --> 00:20:13.810
but my sword is a sword-breaker.

00:20:22.660 --> 00:20:24.880
No... Noise?

00:20:24.880 --> 00:20:25.910
Why?!

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:27.030
Chris-chan!

00:20:27.030 --> 00:20:28.540
I know.

00:20:28.940 --> 00:20:31.290
I'm seeing some old friends here, too.

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:32.790
Signal pattern match!

00:20:33.340 --> 00:20:35.290
I knew it, that unidentified signal 
pattern from last night was...

00:20:36.430 --> 00:20:38.670
I thought the Staff of Solomon 
and the Treasury of Babylon

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:42.360
were destroyed in the trillion-degree heat!

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:47.070
It would quite helpful

00:20:47.070 --> 00:20:50.140
if you would allow me to destroy your sword.

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:54.270
You would expect such femininity from me?

00:20:56.320 --> 00:20:58.770
But my friend once told me that

00:20:59.050 --> 00:21:00.900
the blade of a protector isn't feminine.

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:03.030
I-Is this the time to say that?

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:16.330
<b>Reverse Rasetsu</b>

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:19.840
It doesn't matter how many you are.
 I've done this before.

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:21.420
I won't lose!

00:21:36.240 --> 00:21:36.900
<i>My sword...</i>

00:21:46.850 --> 00:21:48.030
What?

00:21:50.840 --> 00:21:54.660
This is your fate for underestimating 
them as simple Noise...

00:21:56.540 --> 00:22:00.500
Do not think you will escape with a mere defeat.

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:02.890
What's going on?

00:22:02.890 --> 00:22:04.970
Their Gears are dissolving!

00:22:05.320 --> 00:22:07.940
They aren't Noise?

00:22:09.990 --> 00:22:11.430
Alca-Noise...

00:22:12.270 --> 00:22:16.270
What will you do, Symphogear?!
